 Starting with an Olympic record in the heats Jones found redemption for her performance in the Athens Games by being a class above her opposition in each of the her three races. The biggest surprise was that she failed to challenge her own world record."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Finishing second behind Jones was American " [:a {:href "/athletes/115676"} "Rebecca Soni"] ". Although had qualified for the US team at 200 metres breaststroke she had originally missed a place at the 100 after finishing 4th at the US trials. She inherited her place after " [:a {:href "/athletes/126768"} "Jessica Hardy"] " was withdrawn following a doping irregularity but only because the qualifying rules would not allow alternate " [:a {:href "/athletes/103352"} "Tara Kirk"] " to be called into the Olympic team. " [:a {:href "/athletes/103348"} "Mirna Jukic"] "’s bronze was the first by a Austrian woman in an individual swimming event."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/93269"} "Leisel Jones"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "1:05.64 (1 h7)"] [:td {} "1:05.80 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "1:05.17 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/115676"} "Rebecca Soni"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "1:07.44 (2 h5)"] [:td {} "1:07.07 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "1:06.73 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/